course: dictionary
lesson: 14981
title: Repeal: ending a law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A law is a rule that everyone in a country must follow. To repeal a law means to officially end it, so that it no longer counts. «Parliament voted to repeal the unfair law.» The word unfair is a clue that the law was bad, and voting is a clue that people made a decision about it. So repeal must mean to officially end the law.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Try «end» in the sentence instead of repeal: «Parliament voted to end the unfair law.» It still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Repeal can also be a noun, meaning the act of ending a law. «The repeal of the rule means the library is open on Sundays again.» The word «of» after repeal is a clue that it is a thing, not an action.
explain: You will see repeal in history, citizenship and news. A news report might say the council has repealed a rule, which tells you the rule no longer counts. The ending -ed shows that it has already happened.
fact: Repeal is a verb and a noun: you repeal a law, or you talk about the repeal of a law.
fact: «Repeal» means to officially end a law so that it no longer counts.
fact: Laws are usually repealed by a parliament or congress, the groups that make laws.
fact: Laws that were unfair may be repealed.
fact: Useful phrases: «repeal a law» and «the repeal of».
exercise: «Parliament voted to repeal the unfair law.» What does repeal mean? | *To officially end a law | To break a law by accident | To read a law aloud | To make a new law for the first time
exercise: «The repeal of the rule means the library is open on Sundays again.» What kind of word is repeal here? | *A noun, meaning the act of ending a rule | A name for a town | A verb, meaning to build | An adjective, meaning very big
exercise: The council wants to repeal the rule about dogs on the beach. Find and copy the word that means to end a rule. | rule | beach | council | *repeal
test: «The government will repeal the old rule next week.» What does repeal mean here? | Write the rule on a board | *End the rule officially | Make the rule stronger
test: Which sentence uses repeal as a noun? | The teacher will repeal the homework rule. | Mia will repeal the rule about shoes tomorrow. | *The repeal of the shoe rule was a surprise. | Tom likes to repeal his fears.
exam: Ben says repeal means to make a law stronger. What is the correct meaning? | Ask a judge to read a law | Make a law stronger | *Officially end a law so it no longer counts | Break a law without being caught
